content.text:
Fixed. The "whitespace cleanup" commit `ba15d0d` had accidentally deleted a real rule block — the `:active` canvas theme override — not just formatting. I restored it in [billboard.css](formats/components/src/components/billboard.css:123), matching the kept `:hover`/`:focus` theme blocks:

```css
@media (--theme-canvas),
(--theme-canvas-high-contrast) {
  .pfx-billboard.-clickable:active {
    border-style: dashed;
    background: var(--instui-focus-outline-color);
    border-color: var(--instui-component-link-text-color);
  }
}
```

The record reads from the generated `component-styles.ts` (compiled from the `.css`), so I regenerated it, rebuilt the package, and re-staged the docs asset.

Verification:
- **`billboard.test.ts`**: all 4 pass (was 1 failing).
- **Full component suite**: 182 passed (41 files).
- **Docs asset**: the restored override now appears scoped — `:root[data-pantoken-theme="canvas"|"canvasHighContrast"] .instui-billboard.-clickable:active` — with zero `@media (--theme-*)`/`(theme:` leaks.

Combined change surface for the whole session: the docs theme-preview fix (`docs/scripts/lib/scope-components.ts`, `docs/scripts/demos.ts`, `docs/package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`) plus this one-block restore in `billboard.css`. The `generated/`/`dist/` regens are gitignored.
